    "narrative": "Today\u2019s roster construction for the Austin Waves centers on leveraging a massive park and matchup advantage in the **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** spots. **Kyle Tucker** stands as our premier start (85.72) against Sugano; the combination of a +14% park factor and the opportunity to face a pitcher with an xERA approaching 5.00 makes him our highest-ceiling asset. Similarly, **Andy Pages** (75.63) benefits from that same favorable environment in the #3 hole, cementing his status as a \"Strong\" start. **Drake Baldwin** rounds out the elite tier (72.03) today, as his role at the top of the order combined with a favorable matchup against Ober creates a high-floor outcome that effectively anchors our daily efficiency targets.\n\nWe are navigating a few moderate matchups where platoon dynamics and SP skill slightly suppress the raw output. **Gunnar Henderson** (51.50) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (51.76) are forced into \"Marginal\" territory primarily due to disadvantageous platoon splits and tough opposing arms like McClanahan and Buehler. The most difficult bench decision involved **Sam Antonacci** (39.73), who fell just shy of our 40.0 floor. While **Sam Antonacci** carries the underlying tools we prize, the combination of facing a quality arm in Imanaga and a lower-leverage #7 lineup spot left him on the outside looking in. We continue to monitor the status of **Jordan Westburg** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** on the IL, as their absence remains the primary constraint on our daily offensive ceiling. Outside of the typical injury maintenance for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, our primary focus is managing these marginal starts to protect our total game caps while awaiting favorable platoon pivots for players like **Miguel Vargas** and **Jacob Wilson**.",
